From cc88ad3ef775066dead5b4f55eb29fb06edeae88 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: logx <iamvarun158@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 09:48:39 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Ship Title on Android (ai.desertant:title)

Title ran only on Apple, through MLX. Android now runs the same published
MLX folder (desert-ant-labs/title v0.1.0, unconverted) on CTitleEngine, a
portable C decoder:

- Loads model.safetensors as MLX packed it: 6-bit affine, group 64, a
  little-endian bitstream per row (checked against mx.quantize and
  mx.dequantize), bf16 scales and biases, mmapped.
- Granite 4.0 dense decoder: embedding x12, GQA 16/4 heads, RoPE theta 1e7,
  attention scale 1/64, residual x0.263, SwiGLU, tied head / 4.
- Byte-level BPE from tokenizer.json (the cl100k split, added tokens), and
  chat_template.jinja checked for shape and rendered for one user message
  with a generation prompt. The prompt comes from Titles.prompt.
- int8 dot products over the 6-bit weights (NEON sdot, NEON, AVX2, scalar),
  a residual second int8 plane by default so activations are ~15-bit,
  4-row tiles, batched prefill, bf16 KV cache, a thread pool over the
  performance cores. Passages over 1024 tokens keep their first 768 and
  last 256 tokens.
- --numerics exact emulates mlx-lm on MLX's CPU backend op for op and
  reproduces its tokens exactly (Tools/title-engine).

Titles keeps its API; on Android it loads through LoadedModel (download,
verify, adopt a directory) and calls licenseOnLoad(TitleModel.sdkInfo)
once the engine is loaded, as the MLX path does. TitleModel.files gains an
.android entry with the same file list. build:android-natives now follows a
symlinked .build-android.
