+```
+
+Pass a directory to `Title(context, directory)` to use model files you already have: the SDK adopts them and works offline. `download()` fetches and verifies the files ahead of time, and `isDownloaded()` says whether they are present. Blank text returns an empty card without running the model.
+
+On Android, Title runs the same published MLX files on the CPU with a C engine built into the SDK, in place of MLX. The engine reads the 6-bit weights as MLX packed them, so both platforms download and verify the same files. It uses int8 dot products over the 6-bit weights, all performance cores and a batched prefill. A passage longer than 1024 tokens keeps its first 768 and last 256 tokens, joined by `[...]`, which bounds the time to the first token on a phone. Apple and Android decode greedily from the same prompt, but different arithmetic can pick a different word where two candidates are almost tied, so the same text can get a slightly different card on each platform.
